{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\geo\\029.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "ii. Activated Carbon: Carbon filtration is commonly used in many home-based water filtration", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[67, 72], [851, 75], [851, 104], [67, 101]]}, {"text": "plants. The activated carbon used in this process is a very porous form of carbon. It acts like a", "conf": 0.95, "box": [[68, 100], [852, 100], [852, 129], [68, 129]]}, {"text": "sponge with a large internal surface area. Therefore, this process can trap a variety of", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[71, 129], [849, 129], [849, 150], [71, 150]]}, {"text": "impurities. Activated carbon filtration is an excellent purification method for removing", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[69, 150], [852, 152], [852, 178], [69, 176]]}, {"text": "impurities like chlorine-based chemicals, some types of pesticides and industrial solvents.", "conf": 0.95, "box": [[69, 176], [800, 175], [800, 201], [69, 202]]}, {"text": "iv.Ultraviolet Disinfection: Ultraviolet filtration disinfects micro-organisms from water. During", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[68, 215], [851, 218], [851, 245], [68, 242]]}, {"text": "this process, water passes through a chamber fitted with an Ultra Violet light source, that is", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[69, 244], [850, 243], [850, 267], [69, 268]]}, {"text": "usuallyaUVlamporbulb.TheUVlightfromthislamporbulbkillsoffanybacteria,parasitesand", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[70, 269], [851, 269], [851, 292], [70, 292]]}, {"text": "viruses present in the water.", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[68, 295], [300, 293], [300, 316], [68, 319]]}, {"text": "LearningActivity", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[87, 370], [283, 370], [283, 397], [87, 397]]}, {"text": "Most of the waste was buried to decay in the past. Today plastics are indestructible by", "conf": 0.945, "box": [[80, 420], [794, 418], [794, 444], [80, 446]]}, {"text": "natural process, so they pile up garbage or is thrown in the oceans, where it killssbe", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[79, 446], [844, 440], [844, 466], [79